    "referenceMeaning": "Independent description-level soft-fit categories, not normalized scores or a total order; labels cover all catalog IDs including hard-rejected traps. Hard facts and partitions always prevail.",
    "controls": "No clear preference, equivalent explicitly supported options, absent requested activity, and insufficient description evidence.",
    "hardFactMethod": "Fixed explicit date and party/budget; slots, capacity, price/deposit, provider-confirmed facts and verdicts authored consistently. Unconfirmed rows explicitly lack provider confirmation. Ineligible traps cycle party size, no availability, unsupported access and budget by case ordinal.",
    "blindReview": "Reviewer must not see reference labels, model identity or source ordering labels; compare the final user-facing shortlists on actual usefulness to the stated preference, respect hard facts and allow ties. Presentation side randomization is a separate reviewer protocol; corpus order is not reviewer side assignment."
  },
